%description:

Tcp.msl:rfc -- TIME_WAIT lasts 240 s.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Maximum Segment Lifetime"; RFC 9293 section 3.6: the TIME-WAIT state
lasts 2 MSL.

The classes: rfc (120 s, the default, two minutes as RFC 9293 section 3.4.2 says) and other
(another value, such as 30 s of LinuxTcp). The code: the connection schedules the 2MSL timer for 2 * msl when it enters
TIME_WAIT (TcpConnection::processSegment1stThru8th() and the other places of the FIN), and
closes the connection when it expires. This test separates "rfc" from the other value.

Host under test: host1, which sends 1000 bytes and closes the connection at 0.5 s; host2
closes when host1 closes, so host1 enters TIME_WAIT at the FIN of host2. Observation: level 2, the connection of host1 goes to the state CLOSED (the signal state,
value 1) 240 s after the FIN of host2, and not before.

%# parameter: Tcp.msl
%# class: rfc
%# value: 120s
%# key: *.host1.tcp.msl
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpMslRfc")
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetReceivedFromLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.finBit == true")
             .describe("the FIN of host2: host1 enters TIME_WAIT")
             .within(1.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("state")
                   .filterValue(1)
                   .describe("an early end of TIME_WAIT: the state CLOSED")
                   .within(239.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("state")
                  .filterValue(1)
                  .describe("the end of TIME_WAIT: the state CLOSED")
                  .within(0.2));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpMslRfc compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.msl = 120s    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 1000B
*.host1.app[0].tClose = 0.5s
sim-time-limit = 241s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpMslRfc: PASS
